  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "A circle passes through the vertices of a triangle with side-lengths \\(7\\dfrac12,\\) \\(10,\\) \\(12\\dfrac12.\\) The radius of the circle is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{15}{4}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(5\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{25}{4}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{35}{4}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{15\\sqrt2}{2}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": "25/4"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1968-p12.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The sides are \\(\\frac52(3,4,5),\\) so the triangle is right with hypotenuse \\(\\frac{25}{2}.\\) The hypotenuse is the circumdiameter, making the radius \\(\\frac{25}{4}.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "The side lengths are \\(\\frac{5}{2}\\) times a familiar Pythagorean triple",
        "A right triangle’s hypotenuse is the circumcircle’s diameter"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
